      text: "There.\n\nThree lines from the bottom of her own page there was an entry that was not on Rooke's page at all.\n\nNot a wrong figure. An extra line. Somebody had written a purchase into her book after the fair copy had been taken, and the hand was doing its best to be hers and was not quite managing the R.\n\nShe sat and looked at it for a while.\n\nThen she got Rooke round, at half past nine at night, and put both pages in front of her without saying which she thought was which, and watched a thirteen year old find it in under a minute and then say, \"That's not your hand,\" and then say nothing else at all, because Rooke had already worked out whose it was and had decided that was Marta's business.\n\nMarta had her initial the page. Two hands, one number, and the odd line out in the open where anybody could look at it.\n\nComponent found: Rooke's Fair Copy.",
